{
  "title": "The while Loop — Repeating Until a Condition Is Met",
  "subtitle": "Indefinite & Condition-Driven Loops",
  "topic": "5.2 • THE WHILE LOOP",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      5.2 • Condition Loops\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>while</hlt> Loop\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      While a <code>for</code> loop repeats for a known number of steps, a <code>while</code> loop keeps repeating as long as a condition stays <strong>True</strong>!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fed7aa; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy: Charging a Battery\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Keep Going Until 100% Full\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Your phone charger doesn't charge for exactly 50 pulses; it asks: <em>\"Is battery &lt; 100%?\"</em>. As long as that is True, it continues charging:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      battery = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">80</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">while</span> battery &lt; <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">100</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Charging... level:\"</span>, battery)<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;battery = battery + <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">10</span>  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Progress toward False!</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Fully Charged!\"</span>)\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fca5a5; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Crucial Rule: The Loop Update Step\n    </span>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Every while loop MUST modify a variable inside the loop so the condition eventually becomes <strong>False</strong>. If you forget the update step (e.g. <code>count = count - 1</code>), the program enters an <strong>Infinite Loop</strong> and hangs!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}